Severity is justified against this app's read-only, disabled-by-default posture. "Confirmed" means traced in source; runtime/unverified items are labelled hypothesis or blocker.

- F-01 (High, test/CI): Release contract tests under ops_brain/rel/tests (runtime_contract_test.exs, test_release_contract.py, release_probe.exs) are not referenced by .github/workflows/ci.yml; CI runs only ops_brain mix format/compile/test/routes/validate. Evidence: ci.yml steps; ops_brain/rel/tests/runtime_contract_test.exs (7 tests) and test_release_contract.py (backup/restore/migrate scripts). Impact: migration identity, grant ordering, TLS, backup/restore and preflight regressions are not gated. Fix: add a CI job running the Elixir runtime-contract tests and the Python release-contract tests against the disposable DB/roles. Regression: CI must fail on a deliberately broken preflight/migrate script. Effort M. Confidence: High. First seen Pass 1; confirmed Pass 4/5.
- F-02 (Medium, maintainability/security): Two divergent grant definitions. ops_brain/priv/repo/runtime_grants.sql (additive, used by CI) differs materially from ops_brain/rel/runtime-grants.sql (revokes-all-first, requires -v approved_database and ops_brain_migrator identity, adds ops_brain_backup and oban_job_state). Evidence: direct diff of the two files; ci.yml applies priv/repo/runtime_grants.sql. Impact: privilege drift between CI-validated and release-applied grants. Fix: single reviewed source of truth or a test asserting both files grant the same privilege set. Regression: contract test diffing granted privileges. Effort M. Confidence: High. First seen Pass 1.
- F-03 (Medium, security defense-in-depth): Global identity tables (operators, companies, memberships, operator_tokens, oidc_attempts) have no RLS; runtime role holds SELECT on operators/companies/memberships. Cross-company isolation for these depends on application filters (Tenancy.list_companies, Tenancy.authorize). Evidence: create_tenancy_foundation.exs lines 5-53 (no RLS on identity tables) vs RLS loop lines 74-83; runtime_grants.sql line 6; tenancy.ex lines 7-36. Precondition: an application query bug or future unscoped query. Impact: full identity/company enumeration rather than tenant data. Intentional tradeoff (RLS gate covers 17 operational tables), but not fail-closed for identity. Fix: scope-or-view policy or a chokepoint module review with negative tests. Regression: raw cross-company SELECT on companies/memberships raises/returns empty for a scoped session. Effort M. Confidence: High. First seen Pass 2.
- F-04 (Medium, security): Login rate limiter is a single per-BEAM in-memory GenServer; no cross-node/DB counter, and it resets per 60s window. Evidence: login_limiter.ex lines 6-44. Single-deployment posture is stated elsewhere, so impact is limited, but a multi-node or restarted deployment resets limits. Fix: durable/shared limiter or document single-node constraint. Regression: limiter test across simulated windows. Effort S. Confidence: High. First seen Pass 2.
- F-05 (Low, security, intentional dev convenience): Development auto-login is compiled only for :dev and runtime flag-gated, but dev.exs defaults OPS_BRAIN_DEV_AUTOLOGIN to "true" with operator "adam", and any GET issues a session. Evidence: dev_auto_login.ex lines 3-9, 20-50; dev.exs lines 20-24. Precondition: a :dev build exposed beyond localhost. Impact: silent authentication bypass in that environment. Fix: default the flag off or require explicit operator confirmation. Regression: dev build with flag off renders sign-in. Effort S. Confidence: High (design), Medium (exploitability). First seen Pass 2.
- F-06 (Low, security hygiene): Static session signing_salt and encryption_salt literals in endpoint.ex lines 10-11. The real secret is secret_key_base; salts are not secrets but are shared across deployments. Fix: derive per-deployment salts. Effort S. Confidence: Medium. First seen Pass 2.
